        "heading": "Designing your kit in the builder",
        "intro": "",
        "html": "<h2>1. Base</h2>\n<p>Choose a jersey, shorts, pants, or a full kit (jersey plus shorts or pants). Pick long or short sleeves and the collar. Long sleeves are needed for elbow padding.</p>\n<h2>2. Colours</h2>\n<p>Choose <strong>main</strong>, <strong>sleeves and side panels</strong>, and <strong>trim</strong> (collar, cuffs, hems). Patterns use your sleeve colour.</p>\n<p>Keeper kit should stand out from both teams. Bright colours (volt, orange, pink, sky) are easy for defenders to find and hard for strikers to ignore. If your club has a keeper colour rule, follow it.</p>\n<h2>3. Name and number</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Numbers from 0 to 99. The builder warns you if the number colour will be hard to read from a distance. If it does, add an outline or pick a contrasting colour.</li>\n<li>Names use letters, spaces, full stops, apostrophes and hyphens, up to the length our manufacturer can print.</li>\n<li>The preview approximates the print font. Your proof shows the exact one.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>4. Crest</h2>\n<p>Use a simple shield or circle with your initials, or pick <strong>Our club crest</strong>. After you order, we email you for the artwork (vector or high-resolution PNG) and put it on your proof.</p>\n<h2>5. Padding</h2>\n<p>Pick zones for the jersey (elbows) and the shorts or pants (hips, tailbone, thighs, and knees on pants only). Press <strong>Show padding</strong> to see them on the preview. Not sure what you need? <a href=\"/blogs/guides/goalkeeper-padding-explained\">Read the padding guide →</a></p>\n<h2>6. Size and order</h2>\n<p>Choose sizes. Check the price breakdown and <strong>lead time</strong>, then tick the confirmation box and add to cart. You can <strong>save</strong> your design on your device, or <strong>copy a link</strong> to send to a coach or open on another device.</p>\n<h2>What happens next</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>We email a <strong>proof</strong> within [TBC] working days.</li>\n<li>You reply to approve it or ask for changes. <strong>Nothing is made until you approve.</strong></li>\n<li>We make it and ship it. The lead time shown before you paid is the one we work to.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Ordering for five or more keepers? Use <a href=\"/pages/team-orders\">team orders →</a> instead.</p>",
        "narrow": true,
        "tone": "ink",
        "padding_top": 96,
        "padding_bottom": 96
      }
    },
